# Day 26: your first triples, written by hand.
#
# Burger Barn is a made-up burger restaurant. This file says what is inside it.
# Every line is ONE triple:   subject   predicate   object   .
#   subject:   the thing we talk about
#   predicate: the relationship
#   object:    the other thing (or a value)
# The dot at the end closes the triple. Everything after a # is a comment.
#
# Each name is a full web address (an IRI) in angle brackets. It does not have to exist
# on the web: it is just a name nobody else will use by accident. Long, isn't it?
# Tomorrow's file uses prefixes to shorten them.
#
# WARNING: there is one deliberate typo in this file. Day 26's script helps you find it.

# The restaurant contains a kitchen.
<https://example.org/burger-barn#BurgerBarn> <https://example.org/burger-barn#contains> <https://example.org/burger-barn#Kitchen> .

# The kitchen contains a fryer, a walk-in cooler and a grill.
<https://example.org/burger-barn#Kitchen> <https://example.org/burger-barn#contains> <https://example.org/burger-barn#Fryer_1> .
<https://example.org/burger-barn#Kitchen> <https://example.org/burger-barn#contains> <https://example.org/burger-barn#WalkInCooler> .
<https://example.org/burger-barn#Kitchen> <https://example.org/burger-barn#contians> <https://example.org/burger-barn#Grill> .

# Each piece of equipment has a temperature sensor point (like an AHU has points).
<https://example.org/burger-barn#Fryer_1> <https://example.org/burger-barn#hasPoint> <https://example.org/burger-barn#Fryer_1_OilTemp> .
<https://example.org/burger-barn#WalkInCooler> <https://example.org/burger-barn#hasPoint> <https://example.org/burger-barn#Cooler_AirTemp> .
